            <ArticleTitle>Anomalous coronary to pulmonary artery fistula and aneurysm in an 86-year-old female.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>188-90</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>An anomalous coronary artery to pulmonary artery fistula with concomitant aneurysmal dilation is quite rare, especially in the elderly. We present a case report of an 86-year-old female who presented with congestive heart failure from severe mitral regurgitation and was found to have such a coronary anomaly on preoperative angiography. The natural history, diagnosis, and treatment options are discussed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
